# 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Build the application, not just a design mockup.
2. Do not stop after creating the landing page.
3. Do not create buttons that look functional but do nothing.
4. Do not use fake success messages for operations that were not completed.
5. Use Supabase for real persistence, authentication and realtime features wherever credentials are available.
6. Do not expose API keys or privileged credentials in frontend code.
7. Use mock AI only because this MVP explicitly requires it.
8. Keep the mock AI implementation replaceable by a real AI provider.
9. Use demo mode only when necessary and label it clearly.
10. Do not claim that mock functionality is connected to a real AI service.
11. Use reusable components and feature-based architecture.
12. Implement responsive desktop and mobile layouts.
13. Preserve existing working project functionality if a starter project already exists.
14. Do not waste time installing unnecessary libraries.
15. Prioritize functional features and visual quality together.
16. Test the main user journeys before finishing.
17. Never invent external API credentials, database credentials or service connections.
18. Do not introduce unnecessary microservices.

**Execution priority:** A smaller number of genuinely working features is better than many incomplete features.

